## Background and Motivation

Right now there's no syntax sugar for configuring the host options. For example configuring the shutdown timeout looks like this:

```C#
using var host = new HostBuilder()
    .ConfigureServices(servies =>
    {
        servies.Configure<HostOptions>(o =>
        {
            o.ShutdownTimeout = TimeSpan.FromMinutes(10);
        });
    })
    .Build();

host.Run();
```

We should have a simpler way to configure host settings so they are more discoverable.

## Proposed API

Please provide the specific public API signature diff that you are proposing. For example:
```diff
namespace Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting
{
    public static class HostingHostBuilderExtensions
    {
+        public static IHostBuilder ConfigureHostOptions(this IHostBuilder hostBuilder, Action<HostOptions> configure);
    }
}
```

## Usage Examples

``` C#
using var host = new HostBuilder()
    .ConfigureHostOptions(o =>
    {
        o.ShutdownTimeout = TimeSpan.FromMinutes(10);
    })
    .Build();

host.Run();
```

## Alternative Designs

More first class support for options like ShutdownTimeout:

```C#
using var host = new HostBuilder()
    .UseShutdownTimeout(TimeSpan.FromMinutes(10))
    .Build();

host.Run();
```

The only downside is that we'd need methods for every top level option (like the new one here https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/43637)

## Risks

None.

